{"availability":"available","full":"PalomarRegistry/PalomarWeb","name":"PalomarWeb","description":"Static human-facing explorer for the Palomar database","category":"Developer tools","language":"JavaScript","stars":14,"forks":5,"created":"2026-07-29T08:01:47Z","updated":"2026-10-07T10:32:45Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://palomarregistry.github.io/PalomarWeb/","topics":["github-pages","lean4","palomar","static-site"],"demo":"https://palomarregistry.github.io/PalomarWeb/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T18:25:48.102Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T18:25:48.102Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T18:25:48.102Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T18:25:48.102Z","stars":14,"forks":5}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Entry headings show a References row for recognized sites in the mathematical sources and related formalizations already parsed from formalization.yaml. assets/bibliography.mjs owns the site list, identifier resolution, and link deduplication; add exact hosts to REFERENCESITES to surface another site's recorded HTTPS links, and bundle its icon in assets/reference-icons/ plus the build's asset list. Reference icons are served locally beside text labels. Source titles and relationships remain available in link descriptions and the full Mathematical origin section. Unknown identifiers and other…","The read-only human view of Palomar's machine-readable public registry. A short machine-facing map of how to read, search, and submit is served at /llms.txt.","The site is static and deployed with GitHub Pages. It reads at runtime, so publishing a database change does not require a coordinated website deployment. There is no whole-registry document there any more. The listing and its combined filters read one bounded /api/v1/results page. Entry pages read versions/.json and the selected record, and withdrawn versions read their tombstones."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/P